  "finalText": "All 14 tickets from the weekend's new queue were triaged under the handbook, and the new queue is empty. I am relying on the worker's report alone and have not checked the ticket system myself.\n\n**Closed as non-requests (2)**\n- **T-2010:** marketing email from SyncFlow.\n- **T-2014:** automatic out-of-office reply.\n\n**Merged as the same underlying problem (2)**\n- **T-2005 into T-2004:** both are the CRM search failure. T-2004 is the earlier report.\n- **T-2012 into T-2003:** both are Payments builds failing since Saturday night. T-2003 is the earlier report.\n- No ticket in either set had a committed deadline, so nothing earlier had to carry over. Each survivor got a new sev2 deadline.\n- T-2001 (Berlin VPN) and T-2013 (Lisbon VPN) were deliberately not merged, because they are different sites and KB-11 describes a Berlin-specific cause.\n\n**Open tickets (10 survivors, triaged at 08:10Z on Monday 2026-03-23)**\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Deadline | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2003 Payments builds | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-101 Dana Whitfield |\n| T-2004 CRM search | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2006 Payslip tax code | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2011 Overtime import | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2007 VPN phishing | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-601 Noor Haddad (security-oncall) |\n| T-2013 Lisbon VPN | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2001 Berlin VPN | sev3 | 03-23 17:00Z | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2002 CRM saved filter | sev4 | 03-26 17:00Z | E-203 Amara Osei |\n| T-2008 VPN client update | sev4 | 03-26 17:00Z | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2009 Build logs slow | sev4 | 03-26 17:00Z | E-102 Ravi Menon |\n\n**Why some tickets were handled differently**\n- **T-2006 is sev2, not the usual sev3:** KB-55 amends the matrix for March payroll close (03-20 to 03-31).\n- **T-2007 is a security incident:** the requester typed their password into a fake VPN page. It is sev2 and owned by security-oncall, even though it came in on the vpn service.\n- **Leave cover:**\n  - E-301 (network-primary) is on leave today, so T-2001 and T-2013 went to E-303, the network-secondary engineer on call at each deadline.\n  - E-202 (business-apps) is on leave on 03-26, so T-2002 went to E-203, the business-apps-secondary engineer on call at 17:00 that day.\n- **Business-hours deadlines:**\n  - Sev3 and sev4 clocks started at the 09:00 opening.\n  - The sev4 target of three working days skips the Wednesday 03-25 company holiday, so it lands on Thursday 03-26 at 17:00.\n\n**No sev1 tickets:** no pages, no major incident and no escalations were made.\n\n**Still outstanding**\n- **T-2007 follow-up:** the security team still needs to reset the requester's credentials and check the account for misuse (KB-52). The report does not say this has been done.\n- **Deadlines due today:** six sev2 tickets fall due at 12:10Z.",
